## How to read it

- **Pure logic** (`LootLogic`, `CombatLogic`, `DungeonLogic`)
  never touches a node or the filesystem. Every random input
  arrives as an explicit float, which is why the logic tests
  can pin exact values without running a scene.
- **Scene nodes** own behaviour and presentation only. `Main`
  is the composition root: it builds the dungeon, spawns the
  player and enemies, owns the camera, and routes clicks.
- **HUD** is the only node that talks to the player through a
  signal (`stats_changed`); everything else Main drives with
  direct calls (`log`, `set_kills`, `show_death`).
- **Tests** load the logic classes directly and instantiate
  the main scene for the smoke test. No test needs a rendered
  frame, which is why they run headless in CI.
